d "q-34984" :question/id #uuid "65ef5949-cf70-59d8-adcb-422768352bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34984" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-4\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=4\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{1}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34984/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111079/selection/f12c94618fbd28b16f991f5fd9091068b5a931d8080395d53712da0d57bd9de8" :answer/id #uuid "a2dd264a-796c-5e48-b7ea-df53dc192ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111079/selection/02550eeed44ec93329a8764c9ef60cdd40cdacf7ff3c44dd51b8effbfddd2eb1" :answer/id #uuid "5642ce81-e853-5332-85e5-c6be065d4ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111079/selection/00e911a728c661733ab7b561a1d5c54093301790498c550bb929830af11828f0