value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34948"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3k-15 \\\\ -2+k-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3k-15=0 \\\\ k-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-34947/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "5bf0a191-90e7-50c2-bec2-801ced709643" :answ