-academy-id "q-74867" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4k-8=0 \\\\ 2k-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74867/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74867"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection/6f0f1c5837b47c1354b49d5ace51ee1ab0dd84df882f13f1086e4974da6d991f" :answer/id #uuid "8ef04d45-055b-54ab-9fc6-64784f844547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection/5bb2e7270a5668bd79af352c1dd37be2ac4b1fbe4a5490e514690080479548df" :answer/id #uuid "ad2b80fe-f939-58bb-9338-47ef09e9b1f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection/cab8a5715d0321b587d94bacafac03c590f769d3e13364c1070928b4407f0132" :answer/id #uuid "1457ce0e-5a84-5bb5-81bd-e4323eb7d5eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection/88adcd2fc7af5468f6e9af8ba2f6487a0c1db96b1f0b951c67aec0ed95b93ae5" :answer/id #uuid "539e6d1e-d394-5759-8ca2-7e0d84095f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "b51c632c-eee1-515a-bc97-2b6252853576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c4956-7a4b-5521-aeab-1a18c32218cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74870/selection/6f0f1c5837b47c1354b49d5ace51ee1ab0dd84df882f13f1086e4974da6d991f" :answer-field/choices ["q-74870/selection/6f0f1c5837b47c1354b49d5ace51ee1ab0dd84df882f13f1086e4974da6d991f" "q-74870/selection/5bb2e7270a5668bd79af352c1dd37be2ac4b1fbe4a5490e514690080479548df" "q-74870/selection/cab8a5715d0321b587d94bacafac03c590f769d3e13364c1070928b4407f0132" "q-74870/selection/88adcd2fc7af5468f6e9af8ba2f6487a0c1db96b1f0b951c67aec0ed95b93ae5" "q-74870/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74870" :question/id #uuid "352124af-7592-5133-a0e8-40dd6ba11465" :question/math-academy-id "q-74870" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74870/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74870"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection/b3e9cb9c4641399fcc2898e161512b133e00b24dfddb034675b0ca5e6be7325d" :answer/id #uuid "88e3a379-ebaf-5625-96cf-90a97fbae33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection/a6c6562cb68e9c233108eefcadfd649df8d5692f4d3c40a4f76756f5ad7a6b77" :answer/id #uuid "28a46dfc-d92e-5450-9a26-1065cda04b47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "c43b4a17-3d76-5fbf-b2a5-18418608b3be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection/ef2e9d8d7194487409c48123e8865eaeee697ecad86dccfe8b73f2f4e7d263ff" :answer/id #uuid "594b06db-7e4d-576f-91ba-91c6cc56aee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection/399ad9cfe8d527d23c2036163dbd147f0f3814455f7c02061e44f3bd09332225" :answer/id #uuid "9e61b398-3098-5002-b813-6607183debfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "410ee353-55e9-5f9c-b34e-3548f5a62c69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34334/selection/b3e9cb9c4641399fcc2898e161512b133e00b24dfddb034675b0ca5e6be7325d" :answer-field/choices ["q-34334/selection/b3e9cb9c4641399fcc2898e161512b133e00b24dfddb034675b0ca5e6be7325d" "q-34334/selection/a6c6562cb68e9c233108eefcadfd649df8d5692f4d3c40a4f76756f5ad7a6b77" "q-34334/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" "q-34334/selection/ef2e9d8d7194487409c48123e8865eaeee697ecad86dccfe8b73f2f4e7d263ff" "q-34334/selection/399ad9cfe8d527d23c2036163dbd147f0f3814455f7c02061e44f3bd09332225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-34334" :question/id #uuid "d54de9d5-0eaf-51ac-a971-a5633a39368a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34334" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-34334/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34334"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120299 :question/answer-fields 17592186118269] {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "46d0eeb5-f2af-5dea-b8f5-0685c033a445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/62198e20b6e681464385a56ccf985cdf08d11f851a2dd82502307e41496d7d7f" :answer/id #uuid "99cf3227-1b59-53ed-8648-a6af860a94c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/684ab652cfa3c60f0c9d01287ddb788a4fb839bebd898f9c4c82058aee680797" :answer/id #uuid "9d8cbca3-4beb-5ccf-8475-c08ae065e6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/f95b092112bf71b492745397c2e91edc34d2db6d2981efdf82f08fb3a58217ad" :answer/id #uuid "b04dabf1-9b07-5825-a502-057e052d9a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/42414bbbe50a81f8aa05007c09b7a8425bc9db0d53acb78528fed71010a9980a" :answer/id #uuid "eb50163b-9d5d-5ef5-8e38-696c9a4d7bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdc2298c-7547-509a-aafd-8ef518ce57cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/42414bbbe50a81f8aa05007c09b7a8425bc9db0d53acb78528fed71010a9980a" :answer-field/choices ["q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/62198e20b6e681464385a56ccf985cdf08d11f851a2dd82502307e41496d7d7f" "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/684ab652cfa3c60f0c9d01287ddb788a4fb839bebd898f9c4c82058aee680797" "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/f95b092112bf71b492745397c2e91edc34d2db6d2981efdf82f08fb3a58217ad" "q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572/42414bbbe50a81f8aa05007c09b7a8425bc9db0d53acb78528fed71010a9980a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34951"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-34951/selection/ma-v1/e5388fa4eef4220afe75bddc17f222355bc169c896c629c0a99e60447d589572"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120257 :question/answer-fields 17592186118042] {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/47687a8e77a70bee8fcbf5dabcee13b29de3d0b94cbc29192ab625d5830ff6e6" :answer/id #uuid "17c2eefb-f3ea-5112-8fdf-b0744079cbf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/23a1ae6a6be47f112d1d5074083c0bea31f05e3414017b418e4d0ce0e11629a0" :answer/id #uuid "013fca74-c93d-5f9a-b622-75e18c6e670b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/d1f036b834ee843895bef488db1031d9acb1f8748afb37d873cf004f010ecd87" :answer/id #uuid "f53ab6fe-63d7-5f6d-a66f-2f12cb3f33e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "8bd71ab1-7480-5dfc-837d-3ea7ddf44555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/d9cb0e968b49f15534a1e6dca39db3a8f95c234de86d0f7609a5a773d0d3af99" :answer/id #uuid "fb23f712-a66c-540f-8f53-ea184c6a2b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f73e1a5-c789-5447-8de5-7aaa900fe128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/d9cb0e968b49f15534a1e6dca39db3a8f95c234de86d0f7609a5a773d0d3af99" :answer-field/choices ["q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/47687a8e77a70bee8fcbf5dabcee13b29de3d0b94cbc29192ab625d5830ff6e6" "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/23a1ae6a6be47f112d1d5074083c0bea31f05e3414017b418e4d0ce0e11629a0" "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/d1f036b834ee843895bef488db1031d9acb1f8748afb37d873cf004f010ecd87" "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" "q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b/d9cb0e968b49f15534a1e6dca39db3a8f95c234de86d0f7609a5a773d0d3af99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34333"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-34333/selection/ma-v1/369e86bb66331c0c898cd84ec16361897664465ea13328fad84ccf1b64eca66b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection/ec4cde637587e109c386554444e04fe70875e30e06361fbd7a41660fe3baf71d" :answer/id #uuid "961a0716-9c5e-5e4d-b1cf-8aea790908f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "9e76bced-10a6-5e0c-8673-9b861562bf60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection/5a700b0813089908cb7c203f9a7e3f65768a7c0c7dd0c19197d110d92526f4aa" :answer/id #uuid "4a180622-23ec-50c0-8a59-b1ba3b941533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection/13d0b6fdcb95ec4a8328d0378b837f2401bce409c3f6886c0831728a4fc0d4ac" :answer/id #uuid "70d2ab91-f71f-509e-8130-e1b9b95aa016" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection/c05403ae5ad991f278f536201de33df1b01f95d1a5f2586b474d4e7812307f62" :answer/id #uuid "bc1a128d-3b94-5156-a770-06112ace0ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f384dc46-23e6-5c81-87c7-014cacbe321b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74872/selection/13d0b6fdcb95ec4a8328d0378b837f2401bce409c3f6886c0831728a4fc0d4ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-74872/selection/ec4cde637587e109c386554444e04fe70875e30e06361fbd7a41660fe3baf71d" "q-74872/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" "q-74872/selection/5a700b0813089908cb7c203f9a7e3f65768a7c0c7dd0c19197d110d92526f4aa" "q-74872/selection/13d0b6fdcb95ec4a8328d0378b837f2401bce409c3f6886c0831728a4fc0d4ac" "q-74872/selection/c05403ae5ad991f278f536201de33df1b01f95d1a5f2586b474d4e7812307f62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74872" :question/id #uuid "c1241fbe-f91a-51dc-8cf4-08074a70bd68" :question/math-academy-id "q-74872" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4810"] :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/9832b17728be69381a5f534317c0f30156fd32f3706f4cd4634765a02370180e.png)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4812"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/a8b13d238a1e77d90abe70a505c68a72060ea95fe545f56ae53e7cf40ba0595e.png) and the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/6e9f6c010c3137438923dfc32674dedf6d2d554b9b0a6745b007d826954d1e65.png) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4814"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/787a2e53b8e39e79e0e4a2379082187a445a9c6babe0677fa315c516c01f0f67.png) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/f73d7951a041c633d78d1d6971a3473800727452bb92e1b39ad574a045e1b76f.png) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
